9
00:00:40,204 --> 00:00:44,994
Sakai-san from the Sakai family, and you know, the one from the big city...

10
00:00:45,464 --> 00:00:46,994
Is it Kazuma-san?

11
00:00:46,994 --> 00:00:47,914
Yeah, that's right.

12
00:00:47,914 --> 00:00:50,594
The kid that comes by my store once in a while.

13
00:00:50,594 --> 00:00:53,024
But, why on Earth did Kazuma-san have a...

14
00:00:53,024 --> 00:00:55,674
...tug-of-war contest with the father of the Sakai family?

15
00:00:55,674 --> 00:01:01,254
Ah, well... I only came because I heard of the event from the master...

16
00:01:01,254 --> 00:01:06,554
I only came because I heard of it from Yorozuya Inn's Nakai-san, but I didn't hear any specifics...

17
00:01:06,554 --> 00:01:11,764
You people came here all fired up without knowing anything?

18
00:01:11,764 --> 00:01:16,784
For ages, tug-of-war contests have always been about trying to win the hand of someone's daughter.

19
00:01:16,784 --> 00:01:18,304
Eh? Then...

20
00:01:18,304 --> 00:01:22,324
My guess is that Kazuma-kun tried to ask for her hand in marriage,

21
00:01:22,324 --> 00:01:24,834
and Sakai's father doesn't want to let her go.

22
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:29,344
I see, so they had this tug-of-war to decide who gets the only daughter.

23
00:01:29,344 --> 00:01:30,734
This is so nostalgic.

24
00:01:30,734 --> 00:01:35,384
When I tried to ask for my wife's hand in
marriage, her father was really against it,

25
00:01:35,384 --> 00:01:40,194
and it came down to using the
tug-of-war contest to decide the result.

26
00:01:40,194 --> 00:01:44,074
Back then, tug-of-war was called the "Boring Pull", and...

27
