132
00:04:45,644 --> 00:04:47,444
so please go inside and see her.

133
00:04:50,614 --> 00:04:52,614
Ah, I see.

134
00:04:54,454 --> 00:04:56,954
She hasn't been feeling well ever since the tug-of-war contest.

135
00:04:56,954 --> 00:04:58,144
Yeah...

136
00:04:58,144 --> 00:04:59,824
Well, that must be it.

137
00:04:59,824 --> 00:05:01,454
Kazuma-kun would be the reason.

138
00:05:01,454 --> 00:05:02,454
What?!

139
00:05:02,454 --> 00:05:04,254
You're saying Kazuma did something to Madoka?

140
00:05:04,564 --> 00:05:05,414
Eh?

141
00:05:05,414 --> 00:05:07,634
Ah, that's not it.

142
00:05:07,634 --> 00:05:09,344
Listen up, Koyori-chan.

143
00:05:09,344 --> 00:05:15,634
TL Note: He changes "tsuna" (rope) to "tsuma[ran]" (boring), making a pun.

144
00:05:09,344 --> 00:05:15,634
The tug-of-war before the altar has been called the "Boring Pull". It's a pun on "rope" and "boring"...

145
00:05:18,184 --> 00:05:19,054
Ahem.

146
00:05:19,554 --> 00:05:28,064
Thank you, everyone, for taking part in this "Last Minute Summer Homework Rush" emergency meeting!

147
00:05:28,064 --> 00:05:33,324
In order to enjoy the remainder of our summer holiday properly, we should collect our homework and brainstor-

148
00:05:33,324 --> 00:05:34,114
Kazuma!

149
00:05:34,114 --> 00:05:35,864
Are you here?!

150
00:05:35,864 --> 00:05:38,324
I'm here. What's wrong?

151
00:05:42,374 --> 00:05:43,204
Kazuma!

152
00:05:44,334 --> 00:05:46,584
You...

153
00:05:50,504 --> 00:05:52,844
Are you really getting married to Hina?!

154
00:05:53,214 --> 00:05:54,054
Huh?

155
00:05:54,054 --> 00:05:55,054
Married?

156
00:06:02,104 --> 00:06:03,144
Now I get it.

157
00:06:03,644 --> 00:06:06,644
Kazuma and Hina aren't getting married.

158
00:06:06,644 --> 00:06:08,104
Of course not!

159
00:06:08,104 --> 00:06:10,154
How could you even think of
something like that in the first place...

160
00:06:10,484 --> 00:06:12,124
But, I didn't know that you were in a tug-of-war contest.

161
00:06:12,124 --> 00:06:16,154
If you had told me about it, I would have cheered for you.

162
00:06:16,154 --> 00:06:17,704
Ah, well...

163
00:06:17,704 --> 00:06:20,704
Showing your half-naked body and fighting for your senpai,

164
00:06:20,704 --> 00:06:22,384
you have a surprisingly good side to you.

165
00:06:23,164 --> 00:06:28,464
It can't be helped that I was in Hawaii and couldn't be there...

166
00:06:28,464 --> 00:06:32,634
As Fast-Ears Toudou Kasane, I regret it a lot...

167
00:06:33,044 --> 00:06:36,594
Onii-chan used all of his strength, and he was very cool.

168
00:06:37,014 --> 00:06:39,974
Ah, hey. Don't say anything unnecessary.

169
00:06:39,974 --> 00:06:43,014
Okay, I'll go tell Madoka what really happened.

170
00:06:43,014 --> 00:06:43,894
Huh?

171
00:06:43,894 --> 00:06:45,604
Why to Madoka-chan?

172
00:06:45,604 --> 00:06:46,684
Yep!

173
00:06:46,684 --> 00:06:49,644
Ever since the tug-of-war, Madoka hasn't been feeling well,

174
00:06:49,644 --> 00:06:53,364
and Gen-jii told me it was because she thought that Kazuma and Hina were getting married.

175
00:06:53,364 --> 00:06:55,274
If she knows that's not the case, she'll definitely-

176
00:06:55,274 --> 00:06:56,444
Hold on a second!

177
00:06:56,944 --> 00:06:59,404
So basically... that means...

178
00:06:59,404 --> 00:07:01,574
...Madoka-chan likes Kazuma?!

179
00:07:02,284 --> 00:07:03,244
Eh?!

180
00:07:09,294 --> 00:07:11,124
Is that so?!

181
00:07:11,124 --> 00:07:13,424
If you were to ask me, it'd make me feel weird...

182
00:07:14,004 --> 00:07:17,384
Actually, you came here without knowing that?

183
00:07:17,384 --> 00:07:20,554
Koyo-nee tends to not think things through.

184
00:07:20,934 --> 00:07:24,144
A-Anyway, I'm going to tell Madoka!

185
00:07:24,144 --> 00:07:26,354
Hey, Koyori!

186
00:07:28,724 --> 00:07:30,314
And there they go.

187
00:07:30,814 --> 00:07:31,814
Hmm.

188
00:07:31,814 --> 00:07:34,614
Thing are getting pretty interesting.

189
00:07:34,614 --> 00:07:36,114
I think so, too.

190
00:07:39,234 --> 00:07:40,494
So, what is it?

191
00:07:41,034 --> 00:07:42,614
Calling us out here in this heat.

192
00:07:43,204 --> 00:07:45,414
If it's anything stupid, you're in for it.

193
00:07:45,414 --> 00:07:46,534
That's right!

194
00:07:46,534 --> 00:07:49,584
If it's anything stupid, it's cold and sweet and it's delicious!

195
00:07:49,874 --> 00:07:54,004
Ui, decide whether you want to
complain or talk about your parfait.

196
00:07:54,384 --> 00:07:56,964
Daigo-senpai, more importantly...

197
00:07:56,964 --> 00:07:58,424
Ah, that's right.

198
00:07:58,964 --> 00:08:04,874
Actually, for this discussion, I'm thinking about
bringing Madoka-chan and my bro together.

199
00:08:04,874 --> 00:08:06,644
And, I want everyone to help out.

200
00:08:06,974 --> 00:08:09,934
We all know that Madoka-chan is a well developed girl,

201
00:08:09,934 --> 00:08:14,274
and even though my bro is from the city, he's a surprisingly innocent boy.

202
00:08:14,274 --> 00:08:18,024
So, as his friends, let's be the Love Cupids-

203
00:08:18,024 --> 00:08:18,824
Hmph.

204
00:08:18,824 --> 00:08:19,824
Nonsense.

205
00:08:19,824 --> 00:08:22,614
Hinata, you're against this?

206
00:08:22,614 --> 00:08:25,414
It doesn't matter if I'm for or against it. Why do I have to do it in the first place?

207
00:08:25,994 --> 00:08:27,534
What do you mean, "why"?

208
00:08:27,534 --> 00:08:29,084
Isn't it because we're their friends?

209
00:08:29,084 --> 00:08:31,294
Doing things like this is normal.

210
00:08:32,164 --> 00:08:34,964
Anyway, I'm not going to help you guys.

211
00:08:34,964 --> 00:08:37,464
Ah, Ibuki-chan!

212
00:08:48,804 --> 00:08:49,724
Wait!

213
00:08:49,724 --> 00:08:51,934
Wait up, Ibuki-chan!

214
00:08:57,484 --> 00:08:59,314
What's wrong, Ibuki-chan?

215
00:08:59,314 --> 00:09:01,824
This really isn't like you.

216
00:09:02,994 --> 00:09:04,324
Ui...

217
00:09:04,324 --> 00:09:06,034
Ui, you're fine with that?

218
00:09:06,414 --> 00:09:09,034
Bringing that guy together with Madoka-chan.

219
00:09:09,784 --> 00:09:11,994
That's... Well...

220
00:09:12,544 --> 00:09:18,214
To me, Kazu-kun is like a brother...

221
00:09:18,714 --> 00:09:20,674
So, well...

222
00:09:26,014 --> 00:09:27,344
Okay.

223
00:09:27,344 --> 00:09:28,934
If you're fine with that, then it's all right.

224
00:09:30,184 --> 00:09:32,514
Ibuki-chan?

225
00:09:33,144 --> 00:09:35,934
You want me to date Kazuma-san?!

226
00:09:35,934 --> 00:09:37,064
