Such a great atmosphere, right?

250
00:11:14,204 --> 00:11:15,454
Hey.

251
00:11:15,744 --> 00:11:20,664
I'm fine with it, but did I really have to dress up like this?

252
00:11:20,664 --> 00:11:22,374
Of course!

253
00:11:22,374 --> 00:11:27,504
Since Daigo-senpai and I are already disguised, you have to do the same, Koyo-nee.

254
00:11:39,814 --> 00:11:41,104
Okay!

255
00:11:41,104 --> 00:11:43,854
Madoka-chan, where do you want to go first?

256
00:11:43,854 --> 00:11:45,194
Let's see...

257
00:11:45,944 --> 00:11:47,114
Er...

258
00:11:47,484 --> 00:11:47,614
Jet Coaster

259
00:11:47,524 --> 00:11:52,784
If I remember correctly, the date guidebook had the jet coaster as the first ride.

260
00:11:47,614 --> 00:11:52,784
Jet Coaster

261
00:11:53,244 --> 00:11:55,874
Let's take the jet coaster first-

262
00:11:59,244 --> 00:12:00,954
That's surprising.

263
00:12:00,954 --> 00:12:03,624
I didn't think you'd be too keen on a ride like this.

264
00:12:03,624 --> 00:12:07,294
I'm definitely not afraid of these things...

265
00:12:09,304 --> 00:12:11,344
That's right, Koumoto-senpai!

266
00:12:11,344 --> 00:12:15,804
First off, take the jet coaster, raise the tension with her loud screaming,

267
00:12:15,804 --> 00:12:18,854
and improve their relationship with this event!

268
00:12:26,184 --> 00:12:27,064
Let me down!

269
00:12:27,064 --> 00:12:28,694
I'll fall!

270
00:12:29,024 --> 00:12:32,404
Mum!

271
00:12:37,454 --> 00:12:38,874
Are you okay?

272
00:12:40,954 --> 00:12:44,334
Haunted House

273
00:12:41,504 --> 00:12:44,334
Madoka-chan, are you really fine with this?

274
00:12:44,334 --> 00:12:46,254
O-Of course!

275
00:12:46,254 --> 00:12:49,754
Even though I'm shaking, I am a shrine maiden!

276
00:12:49,754 --> 00:12:52,974
Ghosts are my strong suit.

277
00:12:54,974 --> 00:12:57,804
And, next up is the couple's entrance into the haunted house!

278
00:12:57,804 --> 00:13:01,544
When they go in and become scared beyond their worst nightmares, they are sure to cling together,

279
00:13:01,544 --> 00:13:03,604
and there will definitely be an increase in affection!

280
00:13:21,124 --> 00:13:24,084
Madoka-chan, it's already over.

281
00:13:27,374 --> 00:13:29,214
S-Sorry!

282
00:13:31,554 --> 00:13:33,424
m 140 509 b 152 480 192 468 207 461 285 420 459 380 543 360 642 330 854 327 957 329 1035 323 1194 342 1274 348 1356 354 1521 396 1604 413 1652 422 1743 459 1790 470 1824 488 1757 585 1752 641 1728 665 1673 638 1653 630 1583 623 1445 596 1380 593 1287 582 1118 581 1034 575 960 572 848 579 752 585 680 590 605 596 512 608 467 615 404 618 350 638 320 641 296 650 279 656 257 633 236 650 221 657 194 654 179 660 170 638

283
00:13:31,554 --> 00:13:33,424
Petting Zoo

284
00:13:39,764 --> 00:13:41,184
Kazuma-san, Kazuma-san!

285
00:13:41,184 --> 00:13:42,974
It's eating, it's eating!

286
00:13:43,724 --> 00:13:46,064
Up next is the petting zoo!

287
00:13:46,354 --> 00:13:49,694
Feeding the cute rabbits will result in an awkward moment where their hands make contact,

288
00:13:49,694 --> 00:13:52,654
and thus create a strong bond of love!

289
00:13:53,324 --> 00:13:54,904
I'll feed the rabbit, too.

290
00:14:01,784 --> 00:14:03,164
This rabbit loves to eat!

291
00:14:03,704 --> 00:14:05,414
It's just like Ui.

292
00:14:14,094 --> 00:14:15,764
Whoa!

293
00:14:18,264 --> 00:14:21,604
They do say "The way to a man's heart is through his stomach."

294
00:14:21,604 --> 00:14:26,144
Using a large amount of food, she's bound to capture the heart of the hungry man!

295
00:14:23,314 --> 00:14:26,144
A hungry man

296
00:14:26,934 --> 00:14:28,944
Did you make all this, Madoka-chan?

297
00:14:28,944 --> 00:14:29,854
Yes!

298
00:14:29,854 --> 00:14:32,444
I woke up early, and tried my best.

299
00:14:32,444 --> 00:14:34,194
I hope you like it.

300
00:14:34,734 --> 00:14:38,324
If Ui saw this, she'd be so happy and salivating over this!

301
00:14:39,244 --> 00:14:40,454
I'm digging in!

302
00:14:41,624 --> 00:14:44,244
Hey, this is delicious!

303
00:14:48,084 --> 00:14:49,584
Wow!

304
00:14:49,584 --> 00:14:52,834
It sure is high up here in the Ferris wheel!

305
00:14:55,504 --> 00:14:57,554
Madoka-chan, we had fun today.

306
00:14:58,554 --> 00:14:59,974
Yes, we did.

307
00:15:00,434 --> 00:15:02,394
We should all come here next time.

308
00:15:03,264 --> 00:15:04,814
I think so, too.

309
00:15:04,814 --> 00:15:06,974
Let's come here with everyone next time.

310
00:15:12,774 --> 00:15:14,024
Oh, they're here!

311
00:15:15,944 --> 00:15:18,034
Madoka doesn't seem too happy.

312
00:15:18,574 --> 00:15:19,904
Tch, tch, tch!

313
00:15:19,904 --> 00:15:21,994
That's why being young is such a hassle.

314
00:15:21,994 --> 00:15:22,914
What did you say?

315
00:15:22,914 --> 00:15:24,374
What do you mean, Daigoro?

316
00:15:24,374 --> 00:15:29,794
According to my observations, that is the "shy and wants to keep her distance" symptom after a kiss.

317
00:15:31,374 --> 00:15:33,754
M-Madoka kissed Kazuma?!

318
00:15:33,754 --> 00:15:34,674
Most likely.

319
00:15:34,674 --> 00:15:37,924
Then... are they going to get married?!

320
00:15:37,924 --> 00:15:38,554
Eh?

321
00:15:38,554 --> 00:15:40,554
No, you're thinking too far ahead.

322
00:15:40,554 --> 00:15:42,804
But... they kissed!

323
00:15:42,804 --> 00:15:44,054
Aren't they going to have a kid?!

324
00:15:44,054 --> 00:15:47,394
They definitely have to get married!

325
00:15:50,104 --> 00:15:52,144
W-What's so funny?!

326
00:15:52,144 --> 00:15:54,314
I wasn't joking!

327
00:16:20,384 --> 00:16:21,764
Kazuma-san!

328
00:16:27,604 --> 00:16:29,144
Madoka-chan, what's with those clothes...

329
00:16:29,764 --> 00:16:34,104
I wanted to change my image, so I borrowed these from Koyori-chan.

330
00:16:34,814 --> 00:16:36,564
Are they... weird?

331
00:16:36,984 --> 00:16:39,114
Ah, that's not it.

332
00:16:39,114 --> 00:16:41,074
I was shocked, though. It was very different.

333
00:16:41,994 --> 00:16:44,784
Why did you suddenly ask me out for a hike?

334
00:16:44,784 --> 00:16:47,034
On top of that, just the two of us...

335
00:16:47,034 --> 00:16:48,914
That's because... Well...

336
00:16:50,294 --> 00:16:53,004
The bus is here!

337
00:16:55,714 --> 00:16:57,584
How lucky that we caught it on time.

338
00:16:57,584 --> 00:17:01,254
We would've had to wait a while if we missed this one.

339
00:17:01,254 --> 00:17:03,134
Ah, yeah...

340
00:17:14,274 --> 00:17:17,064
So, this is the path that Ayumu was talking about.

341
00:17:17,064 --> 00:17:20,114
It's more of a hiking course than a path.

342
00:17:20,614 --> 00:17:26,824
Since children can easily climb up the mountain using this course, I often used to come and play here.

343
00:17:27,114 --> 00:17:28,534
I see.

344
00:17:37,084 --> 00:17:38,794
This place...

345
00:17:42,304 --> 00:17:43,424
Kazuma-san!

346
00:17:43,424 --> 00:17:44,054
Hurry!

347
00:17:44,424 --> 00:17:45,474
Eh?

348
00:17:45,474 --> 00:17:46,264
Ah.

349
00:17:56,734 --> 00:17:58,774
I'll lay out the sheet now.

350
00:18:28,134 --> 00:18:32,304
Was that girl... back then... you, Madoka-chan?

351
00:18:40,314 --> 00:18:45,734
I was pretty awkward around boys,
and I didn't play much at the shrine.

352
00:18:45,734 --> 00:18:49,614
So, I came here often to play by myself.

353
00:18:49,614 --> 00:18:55,744
One day, a boy I didn't know came here to play, too.

354
00:18:55,744 --> 00:18:59,914
That boy was different from the children at the shrine.

355
00:18:59,914 --> 00:19:02,504
He was kind, and was a very nice person.

356
00:19:02,504 --> 00:19:05,924
To me, he felt just like my knight in shining armour.

357
00:19:08,384 --> 00:19:14,354
Although we only played once, I couldn't forget that boy.

358
00:19:14,354 --> 00:19:18,434
I kept remembering that time when we had so much fun together.

359
00:19:18,434 --> 00:19:27,114
And slowly, I started feeling like we had been playing every day.

360
00:19:28,074 --> 00:19:32,284
Thinking back, it might have been love at first sight...

361
00:19:34,374 --> 00:19:38,164
If that was the case, you should have just said something when we first met.

362
00:19:38,164 --> 00:19:39,454
That's true.

363
00:19:40,124 --> 00:19:44,294
You're right, but when we met at the shrine for the first time,

364
00:19:44,294 --> 00:19:48,714
it was very sudden. I had no idea what to do.

365
00:19:49,514 --> 00:19:50,134
I see.

366
00:19:50,134 --> 00:19:54,934
So many things happened after that, and you
never had a good chance to tell me about this.

367
00:19:54,934 --> 00:20:03,484
I was hoping that Kazuma-san might
remember me without me saying anything.

368
00:20:05,484 --> 00:20:08,904
I had always been thinking about Kazuma-san.

369
00:20:08,904 --> 00:20:10,994
Even if there was only a one-in-a-hundred-

370
00:20:10,994 --> 00:20:15,704
No, a one-in-a-thousand chance, I had hoped that Kazuma-san would remember me.

371
00:20:16,164 --> 00:20:21,664
I wanted a place in Kazuma-san's heart, no matter how small.

372
00:20:23,544 --> 00:20:27,204
I wore these clothes today because I thought Kazuma-san...

373
00:20:27,204 --> 00:20:29,634
...would remember me if I tried to dress like when we first met.

374
00:20:30,304 --> 00:20:31,264
Sorry.

375
00:20:31,264 --> 00:20:36,094
I didn't realise you had thought of that.

376
00:20:36,434 --> 00:20:40,684
Although it happened when I was little, I shouldn't have forgotten your name.

377
00:20:40,684 --> 00:20:46,734
Back then, your hair was short and you had a totally different personality.

378
00:20:51,574 --> 00:20:52,824
It's fine.

379
00:20:52,824 --> 00:20:57,414
I'm happy that you remembered me this way.

380
00:20:57,414 --> 00:20:58,874
Madoka-chan, I-

381
00:20:58,874 --> 00:21:00,034
I understand.

382
00:21:00,834 --> 00:21:02,254
Kazuma-san's feelings.

383
00:21:08,714 --> 00:21:11,384
Kazuma-san, do you remember?

384
00:21:11,384 --> 00:21:16,224
What you said that day when we were saying farewell...

385
00:21:16,224 --> 00:21:17,344
Madoka-chan...

386
00:21:19,014 --> 00:21:22,974
Could you tell me those words again?

387
00:21:39,284 --> 00:21:41,284
It's strange.

388
00:21:41,284 --> 00:21:47,334
Even though we're not saying farewell, I still feel like crying.

389
00:21:49,294 --> 00:21:51,804
That's right, Madoka-chan.

390
00:21:53,004 --> 00:21:55,884
From now on, we'll be friends forever.

391
00:22:01,434 --> 00:22:02,604
Okay!

